# C++ Standards

Language: C++20

## Memory & Ownership

- Prefer RAII
- Use smart pointers over raw pointers
- Avoid manual memory management where possible

## Code Style

- Classes: PascalCase
- Functions: camelCase
- Variables: camelCase
- Constants: UPPER_CASE

## Performance

- Avoid unnecessary allocations
- Pass large objects by reference
- Avoid copies in hot paths

## Headers

- Avoid heavy implementation in headers
- Use forward declarations where possible

## Safety

- Validate inputs
- Avoid undefined behavior
- Handle errors explicitly

## Anti-Patterns

Do NOT:
- Use global variables
- Write overly abstract code
- Introduce hidden side effects